    description:
        "Two calls, two mechanism designs, for self-enforcing N-party coordination: commit, under asymmetric bonding, locks twice the payment from the buyer and twice the value accumulated at its link from the seller, so that crediting a defector with what it retains still leaves defection self-destructive; resolve, under buyer dominance with atomic resolution, closes the process from one signature and induces a weakest-link subgame among sellers. A formal mechanism-design treatment.",
